🐧 Clustering Antarctic Penguin Species: Unsupervised Learning Capstone
A machine learning project leveraging unsupervised clustering techniques (K-Means and feature preprocessing pipelines) to segment and analyze morphological data of penguin populations in Antarctica.

📂 Project Overview
Researchers in Antarctica collected measurements for native penguin species (Adelie, Chinstrap, and Gentoo), but the species labels were omitted from the dataset (penguins.csv). This capstone project applies unsupervised learning algorithms to group the penguins into clusters based on their physical dimensions and characteristics.

📊 Dataset Features
The cleaned dataset contains morphological measurements and demographic details:

culmen_length_mm: Culmen (bill) length in millimeters

culmen_depth_mm: Culmen (bill) depth in millimeters

flipper_length_mm: Flipper length in millimeters

body_mass_g: Body mass in grams

sex: Penguin sex (encoded into numeric binary dummy variables)

🛠️ Methodology & Workflow
Data Cleaning & Preprocessing:

Loaded the raw CSV data using pandas.

